            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Carter G. Phillips (Petitioner), according to Carter G. Phillips (Petitioner), petitioner argues that 42 U.S.C. \u00a71396a(a)(19) requires Medicaid plans to ensure care is administered simply and in the best interests of recipients, and that Maine cannot use Medicaid recipients as pawns to reduce health care costs."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "371444fbf4748cfe5d6ef524ba2311fe194cbdfcf823f88d4dc2d7099dd76c34",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-371444fbf474-0003-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 54,
                "start": 54
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioner contends that prior authorization of expensive drugs will save Medicaid costs and allow uninsured Maine residents to obtain prescriptions, reducing the likelihood of them becoming Medicaid\u2011eligible."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
